  "pride_metadata": {
    "project": {
      "accession": "PXD050035",
      "title": "Identification of serine/threonine-specific phosphatases that dephosphorylate the co-chaperone BAG3 to mediate protein-protein interactions",
      "additionalAttributes": [],
      "projectDescription": "AP-MS study of the human flag-tagged co-chaperone BAG3 to identify putative phosphatases which can regulate BAG3 function. From the two hits PP1 and PP5, the later was confirmed in a reverse AP-MS experiment. PLEASE NOTE THAT ONLY THE FILES LABELLED 'CORRECTED' BELONG TO THIS DATASET",
      "sampleProcessingProtocol": "HEK293 cells were transient transfected with either a BAG3-FLAG or PP5-FLAG construct and harvested at a confluency of 90%. Proteins were affinity-purified using anti-FLAG magnetic beads, incubated with cell lysate before elution with LDS sample buffer and SDS-gel separation. Subsequently, sample lanes were cut in 16 slices, proteins were reduced using 5mM TCEP for 30min at 56\u00b0C, followed by alkylation with 10mM CAA for 30min at 37\u00b0C and finally digested with 0.005\u00b5g trypsin at 37\u00b0C over night. Eluted peptides were cleaned up by C18-based desalting and reconstituted in 0.1% TFA for measurement. Reversed-phase liquid chromatography-mass spectrometry was performed using the UltiMateTM 3000 RSLCnano system (Dionex LC Packings/ Thermo Fisher Scientific, Dreieich, Germany) coupled online to a Q Exactive Plus (Thermo Fisher Scientific, Bremen, Germany) instrument. The UHPLC system was equipped with two C18 pre-columns (\u00b5PAC trapping column, PharmaFluidics) and a C18 endcapped analytical column (50 cm \u00b5PAC column, PharmaFluidics). Peptide separation and elution were generally performed at 40\u00b0C using a binary solvent system composed of 0.1% (v/v) FA/4% (v/v) (solvent A) and 86% (v/v) ACN/0.1% (v/v) FA (solvent B). Peptide mixtures from in-gel digestion were analyzed by LC-MS using a 1h LC gradient. While loaded at 1% B with a flow rate of 10 \u00b5L*min-1 peptides were eluted in a two stepped gradient starting after 5 minutes at 5% B and a flow rate of 0.3 \u00b5L*min-1 over 24% B at min 25 reaching 42% B after 36 min. Subsequently, the column was flushed with 95% B for 5 min. The The MS instruments were externally calibrated using standard compounds and equipped with a nanoelectrospray ion source and a stainless steel emitter (Thermo Fischer Scientific). Parameters for mass spectrometric measurements on the Q Exactive in data dependent acquisition (DDA) were as follows: MS scans, 375-1700 m/z; resolution, 70,000 (at m/z 200); automatic gain control, 3x10^6; max. IT, 60 ms. Multily charged peptide ions were fragmented by higher-energy collisional dissociation applying a normalized collision energy of 28% and a dynamic exclusion time of 45 s. A TOP12 method was applied to analyze peptides at a MS2 resolution of 35,000, an automatic gain control of 7x10^2, and a max. IT of 120 ms.",
      "dataProcessingProtocol": "Thermo raw files were searched against UniProt human protein database with isoforms using MaxQuant 2.0.2.0 using S/T/Y phosphorylation as additional parameter and MBR activated. Resulting protein groups table was processed in the in house python package autoprot (https://github.com/ag-warscheid/autoprot). MaxQuant total protein group intensities of each replicate were then shifted to the summed mean intensities of each group. The intensities were subsequently normalized by variance stabilizing data transformation (Huber et al. 2002) and the rank sum method, as implemented in the R package 'RankProd' (v 3.11), was applied to calculate P-values for the enrichment of proteins that were quantified in all replicates.",
      "projectTags": [],
      "keywords": [
